1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,500
There were mothers who never crossed a classroom door, nor held a book or pen.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:15,000
Yet they, more than anyone, understood that education is the truest light.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Rising before dawn, their hands grew weathered so their children could have a better tomorrow.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,500
Their toil was silent, passing forward the opportunities they were never given.

5
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:36,000
Standing outside the school gate, their deepest prayer was for us to walk inside.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Though they could not read the letters in our books...

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
...they knew one unshakable truth: learning was our only way through.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,000
With hot tea by lamplight and a mother's blessing—"be strong, my child"—they gave us strength.

9
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,500
The achievements we celebrate today are the harvest of their prayers and sacrifice.

10
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:08,500
Every door we open carries the enduring imprint of their sweat and tears.

11
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:16,500
They never called themselves teachers, yet they were our first and greatest guides.

12
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:23,000
And the wisdom of our mothers will live on, honored through every generation.

13
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:27,000
